# Human / production copy

**`ui-minimal-copy`** decides _whether_ to add text. **This rule** decides _how_ it must sound.

## Hard bans

| Ban | Use instead |
| --- | ----------- |
| Em dash `—` | Period, comma, colon, or parentheses |
| Marketing fluff | Plain nouns/verbs: no _seamless_, _robust_, _leverage_, _unlock_, _elevate_ |
| Tutor voice | No _This lets you…_, _Easily…_, _Simply…_, _Just…_ as padding |
| Essay empty states | Icon + one short line, or nothing |

## Length bar

| Surface | Target |
| ------- | ------ |
| Labels / nav | 1-4 words |
| Buttons | 1-3 words |
| Toast / error | What happened; optional next step |

## Before shipping a string

1. Would a careful human product writer ship this?
2. Can it be cut by 30% without losing meaning?
3. No em dashes or fluff from the ban list.
